course: dictionary
lesson: 11920
title: A pink powder for itchy skin
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Calamine is a noun, the name of a thing. You can often find out what a thing is by reading the words around it. «After the bee sting, Mum dabbed calamine on my arm.» A bee sting hurts and itches, and Mum dabbed something on it, so calamine must be something you put on skin to help.
explain: The clues in the next sentence help even more. «The pink calamine dried into a chalky layer on my spots.» Pink tells you its colour, and chalky tells you it dries into a powdery layer. Put these clues together and you know calamine is a pink, chalky lotion for skin.
explain: Look for clue words like soothe, itch and sore. «Calamine lotion can soothe mild sunburn.» If soothe means to calm and ease, the sentence still makes sense. Swap your meaning in and check it.
fact: Calamine is a pink powder made from zinc oxide with a little iron oxide.
fact: «Calamine» is used in lotion to soothe itchy or sore skin.
fact: Calamine is often put on itchy chickenpox spots, insect bites, nettle stings and mild sunburn.
fact: Calamine lotion dries into a pink, chalky layer on the skin.
fact: In old science, «calamine» was also an old name for zinc ores.
exercise: «After the bee sting, Mum dabbed calamine on my arm.» What is calamine? | A type of sunny day | A sharp pin for popping spots | A kind of bee | *A pink powder used in a lotion for itchy skin
exercise: «The pink calamine dried into a chalky layer.» What colour is calamine? | Yellow | Green | *Pink | Blue
exercise: «Calamine lotion can soothe mild sunburn.» What does soothe mean? | Burn more | Count | Wash off | *Calm and ease
test: «My chickenpox spots were itchy, so I put calamine on them.» Why did the child use calamine? | To hide the spots from friends | *To soothe the itchy spots | To give the spots a bath | To make the spots bigger
test: What is calamine made from? | *Zinc oxide with a little iron oxide | Pure gold | Sand and glue | Sugar and water
exam: In old science books, what can «calamine» mean? | A type of lotion for bites | *An old name for zinc ores | A pink flower | A kind of wind
